Expose the live MapFile to the imager progress callbacks (additive; the
existing run_copy_pass/run_retry_pass signatures and upstream tests stay
unchanged).

An embedder that keeps its own map format (the Android app writes
usb-rescue-map 2, not ddrescue's) can then checkpoint exactly what a pass has
already recorded instead of only at pass boundaries.

The retry pass also bounds every attempt to the sector-aligned initial_chunk:
adjacent failed chunks merge into one NonTrimmed region, so a contiguous
damaged area would otherwise size a single read buffer from the whole region.

A sector that exhausts its retries is zero-filled in the image before the map
marks it BadSector, so a resumed run never leaves stale bytes from an earlier
image looking like rescued data.

